30,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,Oh no! The pilot floor takes up to nine minutes every morning! And those shuffles last for two whole weeks? That's way too much time wasted!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The billing is inefficient. We are paying for empty space, and the cost to move power is surprisingly high for every single change.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The survey shows a huge gap in seat quality regarding light. Also, badge records prove that ""first-come, first-served"" is unfair to those who arrive later.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"As I suspected. The noise levels near the door are significantly higher, and the physio's notes confirm that ergonomic comfort takes days of fine-tuning to achieve.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,I found out that the new joiners learned so much just by listening to us! But the cost to move the power is quite high if we change our minds.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, @Yumi, if the power is expensive to move, we should pick a layout that we can stick with! I can't handle two-week shuffles!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"Exactly. We cannot afford a ""flexible"" layout that requires frequent adjustments. Stability is the only way to keep costs under control.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"Stability is fine, but if we stay in one place, we must decide how to rotate the ""bad"" seats. We can't let the same person sit in the dark forever.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"Rotating seats is a mistake. If it takes days to adjust a workstation to your body, moving every month is a physical disaster. We need fixed, optimized spots.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"But if we stay fixed, we might miss out on that organic learning! The new joiners really benefited from being near different people.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I don't care about ""organic learning"" if it means I spend ten minutes every morning just getting my computer to work! We need a fast setup!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, the cost of re-running power for every ""learning"" shuffle is a waste of the budget. We should prioritize a single, cost-effective layout.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shion, I understand the ergonomic point, but ignoring the light gap is unfair. We need a system where the ""cost"" of a bad seat is shared.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,Fairness isn't about sharing discomfort; it's about eliminating it. We should place the most focused work in the quietest zones and leave them fixed.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"Maybe we can group people by project? That way we get the learning and the stability, and we only pay for the power move once!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,As long as it doesn't take forever to start my day! I want a layout where I can just sit down and go!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"Grouping by project is acceptable, provided the layout is final. Any ""trial period"" with seat changes will blow the budget.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"If we group by project, we must still address the window issue. I won't support a plan where the same people are stuck in the dark.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,I will support any plan that avoids frequent shuffling. The physical toll of resetting a workstation is a hidden cost we cannot ignore.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I'm so glad we're agreeing on stability! Let's just make sure the groups are mixed enough so we still feel like one big, happy team!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
